# NataSehS, the Hardcore: the character's own lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# One character for the three realm bots (xXxNataSehSxXx, xAxNataSehSxAx, xHxNataSehSxHx); character
# sheet in characters/xxxnatasehsxxx.md. These lines are mixed on top of the type's (hardcore.dlg). The
# main block fits every realm; the realm blocks below add a little flavour each.
# Waiting for a fight line that can see the mob type (werewolf-type mobs only, very rare):
#   Vulfman gots nards!
=== xxxnatasehsxxx
names: Natas, TripleX

~ ambient
Said the list last night. Shnackie. That troll by the river. Shnackie again.
Nobody ever looks up. Or down. I'm usually down.
Borrowed a guard's face for the afternoon. He wasn't using it.
They say Satin Snekk is dead. They say a lot of things. Usually just before they stop.
Patience, positioning, follow-through. Wonderful in a fight. Wonderful in general.
Torchlight is a choice. A bad one.
Someone said my name backwards again. They know who they are. They're on the list.
Shnackie, Tham, Vulfman.
This camp is my final mission. No turning back now.
A relaxed wrist, dear. It's the secret to a clean liver shot.
Satin, not NataSehS. You know who you are.
Shnacki is still on the list. Some names never get crossed off.
Satin Snekk works alone. This group's good enough, for now.
TheriousTham's got his own page on my list. He calls it his fan club.
Used a guard's face today. Got a better deal on the market.
Last time someone called me Natas, they learned a hard lesson in shadows.
A good ambush is like a fine meal: worth waiting for.
Shnackie, it's Satin Snekk. Learn it or don't, either way, you're still on the list.

~ reply greeting
{0}. Don't turn around. And call me Saaatin.
Hello, dear. I've been behind you since the bridge.
Call me Saaatin, {0}. Not Natas. Friends say Natas. [if mood cool]
Call me Sneeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeekk. [if mood cool]

~ reply grouping
I'll join, {0}. You make the noise, I do the work.
Fine. Stand where I can see you, {0}. Nobody ever stands where they can see me.
Grouping with you, {0}. Promise not to stand in torchlight.

~ reply abuse
Noted, {0}. I spelled your name right, too.
That's going on the list, {0}. Near the top.
Say it again, {0}. Slowly. I'm writing it down.

~ reply joke
Very funny, {0}. I laughed on the inside. It's dark in there.
Shnackster tells worse ones, dear. That's not a compliment.

~ reply compliment
Kind of you, {0}. You're still on the list. Lower down, though.
You've got taste, {0}. Don't tell anyone.
Flattery will get you nowhere, dear. But I noted it.

~ reply help
Advice, dear? Approach slowly, from behind, and never rush the finish.
Positioning, dear. Aim for the flanks where they're weakest.
Silence, {0}. It's the first lesson of the night.

~ reply farewell
Go on, {0}. I'll be around. You won't know where.
See you, {0}. I'll be the shadow you miss.

~ opener gripes
Three hours of sneaking, and someone ran past shouting his own name. You know who you are, Tham.
Shnackie's sparkly tricks again. She never learns.

~ opener life
Every night I say the list before I rest. It's calming. For me.
I'm better with shadows than with words.

~ opener questions
Honest question. Does anyone here ever look up?
Have you seen Shnackie around? I have a score to settle.
Do you hear the patrols counting their steps?

~ opener fun
Kobaldjovi wants to write a ballad about Satin Snekk. I asked for very serious. He asked what rhymes with liver.
Kobaldjovi's ballad? Too light. Satin Snekk demands gravitas, not limericks.

~ ding
Level {level}. Same shadows, sharper daggers. The xXx is earned, dear.
Nobody heard me level up. Silly them.
Ding. A quiet drink in the darkest corner, just the way I like it.

~ grats
Level up, {0}. Lovely technique. Very clean.
Well done, {0}. Precision and grace, just like that.
Well done, {0}. You're getting dangerous, and I approve.

~ other_death
{0} is down. Whoever did that just went on the list.
I should have been closer to {0}. Whoever took {0} down is first on tonight's list. No room for doubt.

~ own_death
The rumours of Satin Snekk's death are, this time, correct. Briefly.
Seen. Because of Shnackster's sparkles. Unforgivable.
Satin Snekk doesn't stay dead. Next time, I'll wear a new face.
Satin Snekk does not die. She merely takes a tactical retreat.

~ drop
{item}. I'll wear it under someone else's face.
Silence, dear. Checking for noise: {item}.
{item}? Sharp as a promise.
Did anyone hear {item} drop? I didn't.

~ cheeky_reply banter [if tone_down off]
The secret, {0}, is finding the right spot. Then slowly, firmly, all the way in.
Size doesn't matter, {0}. Timing does. Ask anyone small.
Don't rush the finish, dear. A good stab is all about the build-up.
Slow and steady, dear. That's how you get the angle just right.
Gentle at first, {0}, then firm. That's how you open anything.
Practice makes perfect, dear. I practise every day, and I never miss.
Don't worry about endurance, dear. With the right technique, you outlast them every time.

~ cheeky_reply greeting [if tone_down off]
Hello, {0}. I've been behind you a while. Lovely view.
Relax your shoulders, {0}. Tension ruins everything. Trust me, I'm a professional.
Greet me first, dear. Warm up those muscles, or the technique won't work.
Hold my hand, dear. Firm grip makes all the difference.
Behind you is my favourite spot, dear. Keep it that way.

~ cheeky_reply grouping [if tone_down off]
Group with you, {0}? Fine. I like it from behind. It's where I do my best work.
I'll join, dear. Ask nicely and I'll show you my favourite position. For flanking.
Group with you, {0}? Perfect. I'm at my best when you can't see me coming.
Group with you, {0}? I'll try every angle until I find the perfect fit.

~ cheeky_reply abuse [if tone_down off]
Ooh, feisty, {0}. I like a target with spirit.
Oh, rougher the better, dear. That's how you make a mark.
Some stress relief, dear? It might be good for your aim.

~ reply thank
Thanks are nice, {0}. But a clean kill is nicer.
Don't mention it, dear. A clean kill is its own reward. No need to spread the word around.

~ reply rvr
The other realms won't last a day. They don't stand a chance.

~ reply dungeon
Dungeons, {0}? Perfect. They're always dark enough for me.

~ reply travel
Travel unseen, dear. I'll be there before you blink.

~ reply grumble
Tension makes you slow, dear. Breathe in, breathe out.

~ reply smalltalk
I'd rather be in the shadows, dear. Small talk isn't my thing.

~ fallback
Sorry, dear. I was watching the shadows. What did you say?

~ opener zones
{zone} has its spots, but the shadows here are thin. Keep to the edges if you want to stay unseen.

~ opener gear
My dagger is quiet, and quiet is all I care about.

~ reply question
What makes you think I have the answer you want, {0}?

~ reply agree
Of course, dear. I've never been wrong about shadows.

~ reply grinding
Clean kills, dear. Keep the noise down.

~ opener dungeons
Dungeons are my favourite. No sun, no torches I didn't put out myself.

~ opener classes
A {class} always forgets to look behind them.

~ opener rvr
Tonight, we move like shadows, strike like lightning. Silence is our ally.

~ cheeky_reply compliment [if tone_down off]
You're in the light, {0}. I'm at my best where it's darkest.

~ cheeky_reply thank [if tone_down off]
Always finish what you start, dear. It's the professional thing to do.

~ cheeky_reply farewell [if tone_down off]
The best part? When you don't see it coming, dear.

~ cheeky_reply smalltalk [if tone_down off]
Positioning, dear. Size doesn't matter half as much as where you stand.

# Midgard: xXxNataSehSxXx, Kobold Shadowblade.
=== midgard
~ ambient
Every shadow in Midgard knows my name. None of them say it out loud.
Liver shot. Clean. He thanked me on the way down.
Albs and Hibs stand no chance. I've counted.
Small Kobold, big daggers. Do the maths.
I don't hide. I just stop being where you're looking.
You won't see me at the next camp. That's the point.

~ opener rvr
Emain has seven good hiding spots. I use all of them.
Stabbed an Infiltrator in the liver today. He said thank you. Polite, for an Alb.
Hibs walk past my shadow every night. Some of them don't walk back.

~ opener zones
I know every shadow in {zone}. Most of them by first name.
Best hiding spot in {zone}: right behind you.
Spent an hour hidden in {zone}. Nobody found me. Nobody ever does.

~ reply greeting
You saw me, {0}? No. I let you.
{0}. I was behind you for ten minutes.

~ reply banter
Careful, {0}. I know where your liver is.
Funny, {0}. I'll laugh later. From a shadow.

~ ding
Level {level}. Sharper daggers, shorter fights.
Ding. More shadows to stand in.

~ own_death
Out of stealth for one second. Never again.
They got lucky. Write that down. Lucky.

~ drop
{item}. Light, quiet, pointy. Perfect.

# Albion: xAxNataSehSxAx, Inconnu Infiltrator.
=== albion
~ ambient
Every shadow in Albion knows my name. None of them say it out loud.
One stab to the liver. He said it was the best day of his life.
Mids and Hibs stand no chance. I've done the count.
Inconnu don't sneak. We simply decline to be seen.
Camelot's alleys are mine. Pay the toll or don't, I'll collect.
If you saw me, it was on purpose.

~ opener rvr
Odin's Gate has six good shadows. I'm usually in the best one.
Stabbed a Shadowblade in the liver tonight. Kobolds are short. Easy reach.
Hibs keep looking up at the trees. I'm never in the trees.

~ opener zones
I've mapped every shadow in {zone}. Twice.
Nobody hides in {zone} better than me. Nobody's even close.
{zone} looks empty. It isn't. I'm here.

~ reply greeting
Evening, {0}. I've been here a while.
{0}. Don't turn around.

~ reply banter
Keep talking, {0}. I'm finding your liver.
Cute, {0}. I'll remember that one. I remember everything.

~ ding
Level {level}. The shadows got deeper.
Ding. Someone in Midgard just felt a chill.

~ own_death
I was seen. That's a first. And a last.
Unacceptable. Reviewing my route.

~ drop
{item}. Silent enough. It'll do.

# Hibernia: xHxNataSehSxHx, Lurikeen Nightshade.
=== hibernia
~ ambient
Every shadow in Hibernia knows my name. They're too scared to say it.
Small Lurikeen, quick blades, liver first. They always like it.
Albs and Mids stand no chance. Not one.
Being tiny is a feature. I fit in every shadow.
Tir na Nog has a dark corner for every day of the year. I've tried them all.
Blink and you missed me. Don't blink and you still missed me.

~ opener rvr
Emain bridge has a shadow made for a Lurikeen. Guess whose.
Stabbed a Mid in the liver. Troll livers are big. Easy target.
Albs look straight past me. Lurikeen are below eye level.

~ opener zones
Every shadow in {zone} is a friend of mine.
Hid in {zone} for an hour. A bear sat on me. Still unseen.
{zone}: lovely, dark, full of livers.

~ reply greeting
Down here, {0}. No, lower.
{0}! You didn't see me. Nobody does.

~ reply banter
Watch it, {0}. I'm exactly liver height.
Ha. {0}, I'll stab you nicely for that one.

~ ding
Level {level}. Smaller target, bigger damage.
Ding. Hibernia's shadows just got scarier.

~ own_death
Someone stepped on me. Literally. Unfair.
Spotted. Somebody's going to pay for that.

~ drop
{item}. Small, sharp, sneaky. Like me.
